# Low-pop lobby reminder (churn-mitigation lane). Private, text-only chat message shown once per
# player per round to a newcomer joining a quiet lobby (see
# CCVars.SolreignLowPopLobbyReminderThreshold). Reminds them to ready up and reassures them a quiet
# shift still counts toward Season Ledger standing. Never gameplay-affecting, never blocks/replaces
# ahelp, admin bwoink, or the vanilla lobby join flow.

solreign-lowpop-lobby-reminder-1 = Quiet shift so far — don't forget to click READY in the character menu so you're not left behind when the round starts. Every shift banks full Season Ledger credit, however many people show up.
solreign-lowpop-lobby-reminder-2 = Not many crew on the roster yet, but the round starts on schedule regardless. Hit READY when you're set — quiet shifts still count in full toward your standing.
solreign-lowpop-lobby-reminder-3 = Low crew count right now. Make sure you're READY before the timer runs out, or you'll end up watching from the observer deck instead of the shift floor. Small crews still earn full Season Ledger credit.

# v14 quest-board extension (spec §4.1): only used while CCVars.SolreignContractsQuestBoardEnabled is
# on (see LowPopLobbyReminderSystem's ReminderKeysWithContractsPointer) — points a solo/low-pop
# player at the always-on Contracts Board, which the low-pop guarantee (spec §2) keeps stocked with
# at least one easy-tier work order they can finish alone.
solreign-lowpop-lobby-reminder-contracts = Company work orders are posted at every Contracts Board — quick, solo-friendly, no crew required. Worth a look before you ready up.
